This product bundles the following third-party components in the binary
`bin/netcheck-bpf` (Go, statically linked, modules vendored under
`bpfcollector/vendor/`):

  - github.com/cilium/ebpf v0.15.0        MIT License
      Copyright (c) 2017 Nathan Sweet
      Copyright (c) 2018, 2019 Cloudflare
      Copyright (c) 2019 Authors of Cilium
  - golang.org/x/sys (indirect)           BSD 3-Clause License
      Copyright (c) 2009 The Go Authors
  - golang.org/x/exp (indirect)           BSD 3-Clause License
      Copyright (c) 2009 The Go Authors

The eBPF program source `bpfcollector/_bpf/traffic.bpf.c` is built on the
header set under `bpfcollector/_headers/` which originates from the
cilium/ebpf examples and is covered by the BSD 2-Clause License.

Full license texts are shipped in `compliance/licenses/` inside the installed
application directory (`/usr/local/netcheck/compliance/licenses/`).

No third-party Python package is bundled or redistributed: the backend uses
only the Python 3.10 standard library (PSF License). The optional `requests`
module is never shipped; if an operator places one under
`<app_root>/depends/` it is used from the local filesystem only.

Build-time-only tools (not redistributed in the package):
javascript-obfuscator (BSD-2-Clause), terser (BSD-2-Clause), Node.js,
the Go toolchain (BSD-3-Clause) and clang (Apache-2.0 with LLVM exception,
used to compile the eBPF object on Linux).

